  "headline": "Mike Flynn rockets six places as Will Finney keeps an 11-point grip on top spot.",
  "summary": "Mike Flynn’s 58-point Triple Captain masterclass was the week’s best score, lifting Bob Z's Drop Dodgers six places into fifth and level on points with Mark Horton. Will Finney remains top on 214 after 42, but Phil Johnson’s 54-point surge has brought As Shaw as can be to third, just 18 points off the lead.",
  "report": "Will Finney remains the Biddenham Fantasy League pace-setter after Gameweek 3, with 0v3rf1tt3d.h5 on 214 points. A 42-point week was enough to preserve an 11-point advantage over Louis Grimoldby’s Grim FC, who scored 37, while the chasing pack got considerably more crowded behind them.\n\nThe big winner was Mike Flynn. Bob Z's Drop Dodgers posted the gameweek’s top score of 58, with no hits, and flew six places into fifth on 192 points. That puts Mike level with Mark Horton’s Vespa Mo Pedro in fourth, while only 1 point separates Mike from Vaughan Cosbie-Ross in sixth. Mitchell’s 15 points, owned by Mike alone, was the standout differential of the entire league and gave the surge some serious fuel.\n\nMike also deployed a Triple Captain, one of five managers to do so. It was a much happier chip story than Georg Coakley’s: Georgingham Unai-ted scored 10 despite playing Triple Captain, collecting the wooden spoon and falling seven places. David Bailey’s Triple Captain returned 44, Dan Birkinshaw’s delivered 47 and four-place climb, and Hayley Phelan’s produced 52. Vaughan Cosbie-Ross and George Foy turned to Bench Boost, scoring 47 and 53 respectively, while Paul Alexis played a Wildcard for 37.\n\nPhil Johnson was the other major climber, rising five places to third with 54 points. As Shaw as can be now has 196 points, just 4 ahead of Mark Horton and 18 behind Will. Vuskovic’s 12-point haul was shared only by Phil and George Foy, while George’s 53 was the third-highest score of the week. The podium battle is properly alive: Phil leads Mark by 4, and Mark and Mike are locked together on 192.\n\nCaptaincy was largely a Haaland affair, with 19 managers trusting the 9-point return. Will Finney was the designated captaincy genius with Haaland on a multiplier of 2, helping the leader avoid any serious damage from the week’s big scores. At the other end, amy warden captained Palmer for 1 point: a call best filed under ‘character-building’.\n\nThere were differential treats elsewhere. Isak scored 13 for David Tonks and Jamie Mitchell, Tavernier’s 10 belonged solely to James Marshall, Ødegaard’s 10 was an olly barnes exclusive, and Hayley Phelan had Van de Ven’s 9 all to herself. For olly, though, the 19 points left on the bench will sting after a 26-point week and a six-place drop.\n\nJames Geary joined Georg among the biggest fallers, dropping seven places after scoring 17. The league average was 39.5, ahead of the global average of 36, so there was little room to hide. With 35 gameweeks remaining, Will is still the hottest manager over the last three gameweeks on 214, but Mike’s charge, Phil’s rise and the dead heat between Mark and Mike have made the early title picture far more entertaining.",
